    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1373503cce783e528cdb3b21c573faad7b0e45ed9aa0f71f36dbede515e51f24",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The cutoff PQ system and cutoff additive white light are connected by symplectic coordinate changes that preserve phase-space area and pq; under the rescaling, the missing white-light region becomes the Berry-Keating semiclassical region. This transfers the counting picture but not the quantum model, because the absorption minus sign reappears in the Maslov phases of quantum fluctuations.",
