      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_24921bef5b35bc5190800bc9f4610b02ed2e6b6adebc2fc1a25f9cef80dd8d3e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Li's positive-compression route would prove the proposed Weil inequality only if the quantized logarithmic derivative of the local-factor product had the required negative sign, which in one variable is equivalent to the adjoint local-factor ratio being inner. The finite and archimedean ratios fail the needed Hardy-space condition through poles or unboundedness, and the unrestricted inequality is independently impossible because it would force a false monotonicity of the Riemann-Siegel phase.",
