    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_48c8346fa5b1f50a38fc5cbf83f00b8ca8226c0fc9cd0fd4341b9a617f26b4b3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source proposes that restricting test-function support should reduce the Weil problem to a finite semi-local place set, but the failed cutoff argument shows that local principal values cannot be normalized arbitrarily. Poisson summation supplies the missing organizing constraint: it produces the local-factor ratios in Fourier coordinates and makes the admissible basic-character choices equivalent on the semi-local quotient, thereby motivating the normalization-sensitive Conjecture 4.1.",
