      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8da354b28e120215c14d5bc37cc6cc09c7749d603c0952e7cb1c1682d514872c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "On the semi-local quotient, scaling is intertwined with a modulated regular representation. The additive Fourier transform is then expressed, after multiplicative Fourier transform and inversion, through a product of placewise local-factor ratios; applying the quantized logarithmic differential to that product splits the cutoff trace into a sum of local explicit-formula contributions.",
