    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b7f70ff2ab4f8932d5194872c547b2e0fb63c92ce13bc5fedaad23dd9c3556f9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A polynomial in the scaling generator can be chosen to commute with Fourier transform and force the two vanishing constraints used to construct Sonine functions. The source then extends the same scaling structure beyond this analytic construction: finite-field zero ordinates are naturally periodic times rather than energies, the adjoint generator expression enters the tropical Scaling Site, and the global scaling action is interpreted as Frobenius.",
